  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"1.31.9\"\n\npackage:\n  name: nginx\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://nginx.org/download/nginx-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: a11c5eeee2e257f4478f0e649f84b0040787d277d2d3e5233952aa6b6dcb80ad\n  patches:\n    - if: osx and arm64\n      then: test.patch\n    # find pcre in PREFIX instead of /usr\n    - pcre-config.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  skip: win\n  always_copy_files:\n    - etc/*\n    - var/log/nginx/*\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - make\n    - gnuconfig\n  host:\n    - libgd\n    - libxslt\n    - libxml2-devel\n    # mod_zip filename charset conversion\n    - libiconv\n    # crypt() for auth_basic password schemes beyond {PLAIN}/{SHA}/{SSHA}/$apr1$\n    - if: linux\n      then: libxcrypt\n    - openssl\n    - pcre2\n    - zlib\n\ntests:\n  - package_contents:\n      bin:\n        - nginx\n      files:\n        - sbin/nginx\n        - etc/nginx/nginx.conf\n        - etc/nginx/nginx.conf.default\n        - etc/nginx/sites.d/default-site.conf\n        - lib/nginx/modules/ngx_mail_module.so\n        - lib/nginx/modules/ngx_stream_module.so\n        - lib/nginx/modules/ngx_http_xslt_filter_module.so\n        - lib/nginx/modules/ngx_http_image_filter_module.so\n  - files:\n      recipe:\n        - run_test.sh\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - curl\n        - if: linux\n          then: procps-ng\n    script:\n      - nginx -h\n      - bash run_test.sh\n  - if: linux\n    then:\n      files:\n        recipe:\n          - test_auth_crypt.sh\n      requirements:\n        run:\n          - curl\n      script:\n        - bash test_auth_crypt.sh\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://nginx.org\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: Nginx is an HTTP and reverse proxy server\n  description: |\n    Nginx can act as a reverse proxy server for TCP, UDP, HTTP, HTTPS, SMTP,\n    POP3, IMAP, and gRPC protocols, as well as a load balancer and an HTTP cache.\n    Nginx uses an asynchronous event-driven approach to handling requests.\n  documentation: https://nginx.org/en/docs\n  repository: https://github.com/nginx/nginx\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - sodre\n    - fhoehle\n    - pavelzw\n    - hobu\n",
